  "report": {
    "incident_title": "Partners getting 5xx from the tracking API since ~09:00",
    "outcome": "inconclusive",
    "summary": "tracking-api 5xx were triggered by a sudden write-load spike that saturated the tracking-db\u2019s provisioned storage IOPS starting ~08:50 UTC.  Query latency rose from <10 ms to \u22481 s (call-0012), so each HTTP request held its DB connection much longer and the tracking-api pool filled up.  When FinOps lowered the pool ceiling from 50\u219240 at 08:55 UTC (call-0002) the pool immediately hit the new limit (call-0006) and requests began timing-out (wait_p99 \u22482 s, call-0005), pushing the error-rate above 12 % (call-0005) and firing the 5xx and DbPoolSaturated alerts (call-0003).  The pool change worsened the symptom but the underlying cause is the database IOPS saturation, not the pool size.",
    "root_cause": null,
    "confidence": "low",
